.TH HOMENET 1 "2026" "homenet" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
homenet \- beginner-friendly tools for seeing what is on your home network
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B homenet
.RB [ \-h ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-\-show\-cmd ]
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B homenet
wraps
.BR nmap (1)
so you can list devices, ports, and services without learning nmap's flags.
.PP
.B Only scan networks you own or have permission to scan.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit. Each command also accepts
.BR \-\-help .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the program version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show each step on stderr. Repeat
.RB ( \-vv )
to include nmap's progress.
.TP
.B \-\-show\-cmd
Show each real command on stderr before it runs. With
.BR \-\-json ,
add a commands list instead.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B whoami\-net
Show this computer's address on your home network.
.TP
.B devices
List devices currently on your home network.
.TP
.BI device " IP"
Show details for one device by its IP address.
.TP
.B ports
List remote ports, or local listeners with
.BR \-\-local .
.TP
.BI services " IP"
Show the services running on one device.
.TP
.B router
Find your home router.
.TP
.B baseline
Save a snapshot of the devices on your network.
.TP
.B new\-devices
List devices that were not in your saved snapshot.
.TP
.B speed
Check how fast your internet connection is.
.TP
.B wifi
Show the Wi\-Fi signal, band, and channel.
.TP
.B dns
Show DNS servers and try a lookup.
.TP
.B doctor
Check that tools and permissions are ready.
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove homenet from this computer.
.TP
.BI explain " command"
Show the real commands a command would run, without running them. Use
.BI \-\-network " CIDR"
to skip the network lookup.
.SH SUDO
Root adds MAC addresses and makers for
.BR devices ", " device ", " baseline ", and " new\-devices .
.BR doctor ", " whoami\-net ", " explain ", " speed ", " wifi ", " dns ", and " uninstall
do not need sudo.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
homenet devices
sudo homenet devices
homenet explain devices \-\-network 192.168.1.0/24
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nmap (1),
.BR ip (8)
